 36S  c  2025Ni08: absolute intensity of the weak |b{++} branch of {+36}Cl      
 36S 2c  measured with a |b|g-coincidence technique. A liquid {+36}Cl sample of 
 36S 3c  known activity embedded in scintillation cocktail was measured in a    
 36S 4c  4|p|a|b(LS)-|g(HPGe) system comprising a liquid scintillator (LS)      
 36S 5c  detector and an HPGe detector, the LS detector including a             
 36S 6c  photo-reflector assembly that holds the sample and ensures high        
 36S 7c  efficiency for |b particles. Timestamps and energies of the |b and |g  
 36S 8c  events filter out events originating outside the sample volume,        
 36S 9c  allowing clear observation of the 511-keV |g rays from positron        
 36S Ac  emission in a practically background-free environment. The system was  
 36S Bc  calibrated for |b and |g detection with radioactive sources in the same
 36S Cc  geometry as the {+36}Cl sample. Measured E|b, I|b, E|g, I|g, and       
 36S Dc  |b|g-coin. Deduced absolute |b{++} intensity 1.62|*10{+-5} {I15}.      
